BossLore (
    boss_id: "last_star",
    canonical_name: "The Last Star",
    world: "vulcan",
    biome: "stellar_edge_inner_orbit",
    arena_rule: "OneWayCutsceneEntry",
    entries: [
        BossLoreEntry (
            kind: "origin_myth",
            title: "What Was Built Before the Sun",
            body: "The Last Star is, by every available Concordat reading, older than the Sol system. The Collegium's first dating analysis of the surface samples recovered by Captain Hawthorne's 2230 Vulcan day-side expedition produced a lower bound of approximately five billion Earth-years on the structure's age, which is, by all current astrophysics, approximately the age of the sun itself. The structure's purpose is unknown. The structure's builders are unknown. The structure's relationship to the Sol system is, by Collegium consensus, the single most consequential unresolved question in current Concordat research. The Husks have, in their oldest oral histories, a phrase the Collegium has translated as 'the lamp of the world before this world'. The Crystalfold, in their oldest song, have, by Echo of First Bloom's account, a sustained reference to a structure whose nature they have, in fifty years of inquiry, declined to elaborate upon. The Starlight Concordant's classification of the Last Star site as off-limits is, by every Concordat policy review, the only Concordat classification all eight factions have, in writing, supported."
        ),
        BossLoreEntry (
            kind: "war_history",
            title: "The One Expedition",
            body: "The Last Star has been formally engaged on exactly one occasion. The engagement was in 2241 — the present year — by a campaign-final expedition force assembled from the Coalition, the Collegium, the Starlight Concordant, and a single Ronin master in observation capacity. The expedition is, in current Concordat documentation, ongoing. The current expedition is, by every available reading, an in-progress event that any campaign-final player encounter is, in narrative framing, joining. The expedition has produced no after-action reports. The expedition has produced approximately four hundred and seventeen recorded fatalities across all participating factions, and approximately three thousand and ninety classified sensor logs that the Collegium is, in writing, declining to release. The expedition's stated objective is to determine whether the Last Star's archway opens, and if it opens, where it leads."
        ),
        BossLoreEntry (
            kind: "defeat_consequences",
            title: "What the Final Commitment Means",
            body: "The Last Star is, in mechanical framing, the only boss in the Concordat's PvE inventory whose engagement is conducted under the OneWayCutsceneEntry arena rule with no possibility of withdrawal once committed. The player, on entering the arena, commits to the full five-phase encounter. The rewards are the Stellar Forge recipe, the Last Star artifact, and five distinct lore unlocks — the entries below this one. The campaign cost is the highest in any current Concordat campaign: every active save file is, by Coalition protocol, archived as 'expedition committed' upon arena entry, and the player's progress in the current campaign is, after the encounter, treated as final regardless of outcome. The narrative cost is in every framing, the largest the campaign offers. The Concordat does not, in any document, recommend the engagement. The campaign does not, in any narrative framing, require it. The engagement is, in every sense, voluntary. Most players, by current Concordat data, accept the engagement anyway."
        ),
        BossLoreEntry (
            kind: "phase_descriptions",
            title: "The Five Trials",
            body: "Phase One: the player enters the outer ring of the Last Star site. The ring is a defensive perimeter of automated structures whose origin is unknown and whose targeting parameters are, by every Concordat analysis, calibrated to current Concordat technology. The phase tests the player's basic combat capacity at T3+ gear. The phase ends when the perimeter is breached. Phase Two: the player crosses the inner field, a region of magma-vent terrain in which the Vulcan biome's environmental hazards are at maximum operational density. The phase tests endurance, resource management, and the player's ability to survive an environment that is, by Concordat reading, deliberately hostile. The phase ends when the player reaches the archway. Phase Three: the archway opens. What emerges from the archway is, by every current Concordat document, classified, and is the encounter's primary engagement. The phase tests the player's combat capacity against a previously-unencountered category of opponent. The phase ends when the opponent is reduced below the engagement threshold. Phase Four: the player must, in the seconds immediately following phase three's resolution, decide whether to enter the archway or remain on the Vulcan side. Both choices have consequences. The phase ends with the player's choice recorded. Phase Five: depending on the phase four choice, the player either crosses the archway threshold or holds the threshold against what attempts to follow. The phase is, in either case, the encounter's resolution. The encounter does not have a documented victory state. The encounter has, in every Concordat account, only documented exits."
        ),
        BossLoreEntry (
            kind: "dropped_lore_codex",
            title: "The Five Things Said, Recorded by the Concordat 2241",
            body: "Five statements recovered from the expedition's classified sensor logs, attributed to five different speakers from five different factions, recorded in approximately the order given. ONE (Coalition fire-team leader): 'The perimeter is, in this professional opinion, not designed to keep us out. The perimeter is designed to keep something in.' TWO (Collegium senior researcher): 'The dating profile is, in this researcher's professional opinion, consistent with the structure having been here when the sun ignited. The structure does not, in any sense available to current human science, belong to the Sol system. The structure was, in the most parsimonious reading, present before the Sol system formed around it.' THREE (Starlight captain, identified only as 'survey command'): 'The archway is opening. The archway is, in this captain's professional opinion, not opening for us. The archway is opening because the time has come for the archway to open. We are, in this expedition, visitors at a door that was always going to open at exactly this hour.' FOUR (Ronin observer, voice identified by intonation analysis as a senior master): 'The Combine recognizes the carrying. The Combine recognizes what is on the other side. The Combine recites the names of the dead before us; the names have, in this recital, included some that the Combine has not, in two centuries, used. The Combine continues reciting.' FIVE (unattributed, voice does not match any known Concordat speaker): 'We have been, in this place, very patient.'"
        ),
    ],
)
